<section class="page" id="p-about">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="crumbs"><a href="#home">Home</a> &middot; About</div>
  <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#fff;margin-top:14px">About SANTACO</span>
  <h1>The unified, democratic voice of the taxi industry.</h1>
  <p>Born from the National Taxi Task Team process and formed in 2001, SANTACO unites the country's taxi associations under one national federation — the engine behind the nation.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pres reveal">
      <div class="photo pres-portrait" style="aspect-ratio:4/4.4"><img src="https://santaco.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/SA-Taxi.jpg" alt="South African taxi industry" onerror="this.classList.add('fail')"><span class="flabel">SANTACO · official imagery</span></div>
      <div class="pres-body">
        <span class="eyebrow">Who we are</span>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3vw,2.4rem);margin-top:14px">An apex body representing a R-billion industry.</h2>
        <p style="margin-top:16px;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7">SANTACO is the recognised national representative body of the minibus taxi industry in South Africa. It speaks for roughly 300,000 members and 200,000 operators running more than 350,000 vehicles — an industry that carries the majority of the country's public-transport commuters every day.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7">Through the National Taxi Lekgotla and the Joint Taxi Task Team, SANTACO works with national and provincial government to formalise, professionalise and modernise the sector, while defending the interests of operators and the commuters they serve.</p>
        <div class="vm-grid">
          <div class="vm"><h4>Our Mission</h4><p data-bind="mission">To drive the transformation of public transport through safe, reliable and innovative mobility and logistics solutions, while promoting economic empowerment and a diversified, sustainable industry.</p></div>
          <div class="vm"><h4>Our Vision</h4><p data-bind="vision">To be a visionary and progressive taxi council that champions a diversified, transformed, inclusive and sustainable public transport sector.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Our journey</span><h2>From one table in Durban to a national federation.</h2>
      <p>Two decades of building a unified, democratic and representative taxi council.</p></div>
    <div class="timeline reveal">
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2001</div><p>SANTACO formed in Durban; first democratic leadership elected.</p></div>
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2005</div><p>SANTACO Constitution officially signed.</p></div>
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2010</div><p>Hlokomela road-safety campaign launched.</p></div>
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2015</div><p>Women's Desk established; National Taxi Lekgotla participation.</p></div>
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2020</div><p>Apex-body status; Joint Taxi Task Team formed.</p></div>
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2024</div><p>Inaugural National Policy Conference across all modes.</p></div>
      <div class="tl"><div class="dot"></div><div class="yr">2026</div><p>New national executive elected for the 2026&ndash;2030 term.</p></div>
